    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **274 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented city title-casing on owner creation with spelling reuse for existing cities.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/NormalizeCity.java`:\n- Looks up all owners; if one already lives in the same city (case-insensitively), it copies that owner's **exact** stored spelling onto the new owner.\n- Otherwise it **title-cases** the input (`\"riverdale\"` \u2192 `\"Riverdale\"`, capitalizing the first letter of each whitespace-separated word and lowercasing the rest).\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted a `normalizeCity` step between `build` and `checkDuplicate`, under the same `transaction` governance, so the normalized city is what gets saved and returned in the `city` field.\n\nPlacing it before `assignCustomerCode` also keeps the existing per-city sequence (cp10) working, since reused spellings produce exact-match city grouping.\n\nBoth the new `Cp12Tests` (title-case + reuse) and the related `Cp10Tests` pass, and the full 274-test suite is green.",
